# Frontend Development Guidelines

## View Templates (.ct files)
- Use the framework's templating system for views
- Follow the established layout patterns
- Implement proper escaping for security
- Use components for reusable UI elements
- Maintain consistent styling and structure

## CSS Organization
The framework includes CSS files in [Storage/css/](mdc:Storage/css/):
- [Storage/css/bootstrap.css](mdc:Storage/css/bootstrap.css) - Bootstrap framework
- [Storage/css/custom.css](mdc:Storage/css/custom.css) - Custom styles
- [Storage/css/tailwind.css](mdc:Storage/css/tailwind.css) - Tailwind CSS

### CSS Best Practices
- Use consistent naming conventions
- Implement responsive design
- Follow mobile-first approach
- Use CSS variables for theming
- Minimize CSS specificity conflicts
- Implement proper accessibility features

## JavaScript Organization
JavaScript files are located in [Storage/js/](mdc:Storage/js/):
- [Storage/js/bootstrap.js](mdc:Storage/js/bootstrap.js) - Bootstrap JavaScript
- [Storage/js/custom.js](mdc:Storage/js/custom.js) - Custom JavaScript

### JavaScript Best Practices
- Use modern ES6+ syntax
- Implement proper error handling
- Use async/await for asynchronous operations
- Follow consistent code formatting
- Implement proper event handling
- Use modules for code organization

## Frontend Services
The framework includes microservices in [Services/](mdc:Services/):
- [Services/frontend/](mdc:Services/frontend/) - Frontend service
- [Services/node-api/](mdc:Services/node-api/) - Node.js API service

### Service Integration
- Use proper API endpoints
- Implement error handling for API calls
- Use appropriate HTTP methods
- Implement loading states
- Handle network errors gracefully

## Asset Management
- Use the framework's asset management system
- Implement proper asset versioning
- Optimize asset loading
- Use CDN for static assets when appropriate
- Implement proper caching strategies

## Responsive Design
- Design for mobile-first
- Use flexible grid systems
- Implement proper breakpoints
- Test across different devices
- Ensure touch-friendly interfaces

## Accessibility
- Follow WCAG guidelines
- Implement proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Test with screen readers

## Performance Optimization
- Minimize HTTP requests
- Implement lazy loading
- Optimize images and assets
- Use efficient CSS selectors
- Minimize JavaScript execution time

## Browser Compatibility
- Test across major browsers
- Use progressive enhancement
- Implement fallbacks for older browsers
- Use feature detection
- Follow web standards

## Security Considerations
- Sanitize user input
- Implement proper CSP headers
- Validate client-side data
- Use secure communication protocols
- Implement proper session management